      },
      "message": "fix(setups): re-applied two-axis part picks refuse as already held\n\nalign_from_axes re-composed an identity turn about the part centre onto\nthe held alignment, leaving float noise in the origin that change_of took\nfor a change: re-applying the same +Y/+X picks stored a no-op undo step.\nA turn below a quarter of the landing tolerance now hands back the held\nalignment unchanged, so the GUI's Apply check and MCP set_part_axes both\nrefuse \"already holds the part that way\". Real turns are unchanged.\n\nFixes #1347\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
